#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:20
msgid "Reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:430
msgid ""
"It is important to note the distinction between signed and unsigned types. "
"For unsigned integers, which wrap on overflow by default, "
"`overflow_behavior(trap)` is particularly useful for enabling overflow "
"checks. For signed integers, whose overflow behavior is undefined by "
"default, `overflow_behavior(wrap)` provides a guaranteed wrapping behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:436
msgid ""
"The `overflow_behavior` attribute can be used to override the behavior of "
"entries from a {doc}`SanitizerSpecialCaseList`. This is useful for "
"allowlisting specific types into overflow or truncation instrumentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:440
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:442
msgid ""
"Clang provides diagnostics to help developers manage overflow behavior types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:444
msgid "Specification Errors and Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:446
msgid ""
"When using overflow behavior types, several diagnostics help catch mistakes "
"in how the types are specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:449
msgid "**Conflicting Specifications:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:451
msgid ""
"An error is issued when both the keyword syntax and attribute syntax are "
"used with incompatible overflow behaviors on the same type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:460
msgid "**Redundant Specifications:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:462
msgid ""
"A warning is issued when both syntax forms specify the same behavior, which "
"is redundant but allowed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:471
msgid "**Feature Not Enabled:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:473
msgid ""
"When overflow behavior types are used without enabling the feature via `-"
"fexperimental-overflow-behavior-types`, a warning is issued and the "
"attribute is ignored:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:483
msgid "-Woverflow-behavior-conversion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:485
msgid ""
"This warning group is issued when an overflow behavior type is implicitly "
"converted to a standard integer type, which may lead to the loss of the "
"specified overflow behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:500 ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:582
msgid ""
"To fix this, you can explicitly cast the overflow behavior type to a "
"standard integer type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:513
msgid ""
"This warning group includes `-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion`, which "
"includes `-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-assignment`, `-Wimplicit-"
"overflow-behavior-conversion-function-boundary`, `-Wimplicit-overflow-"
"behavior-conversion-function-boundary-pedantic`, and `-Wimplicit-overflow-"
"behavior-conversion-pedantic`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:521
msgid "`-Woverflow-behavior-conversion` is implied by `-Wconversion`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:524
msgid "-Wincompatible-pointer-types-discards-overflow-behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:526
msgid ""
"This warning (enabled by default) is issued when converting between pointer "
"types where overflow behavior information is discarded. This occurs when "
"assigning between pointers that differ only in their overflow behavior "
"annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:545
msgid ""
"This warning is part of the `-Wincompatible-pointer-types` group and helps "
"catch potential bugs where overflow behavior contracts may be inadvertently "
"lost through pointer conversions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:549
msgid "-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:551
msgid ""
"This warning is issued when an overflow behavior type is implicitly "
"converted to a standard integer type as part of most conversions, which may "
"lead to the loss of the specified overflow behavior. This is the main "
"warning in the `-Woverflow-behavior-conversion` group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:567
msgid ""
"Here's another example showing function parameter conversion with a `trap` "
"type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:603
msgid "-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-assignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:605
msgid ""
"This warning is issued specifically when an overflow behavior type is "
"implicitly converted to a standard integer type during assignment operations "
"or variable initialization. This is a subset of the more general `-Wimplicit-"
"overflow-behavior-conversion` warning, allowing developers to control "
"assignment-specific warnings separately. This warning is disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:623
msgid "This also applies to variable initialization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:634
msgid ""
"This diagnostic can be controlled independently, allowing projects to "
"suppress assignment-related warnings while still receiving warnings for "
"other types of implicit conversions (such as function parameter passing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:638
msgid ""
"Note that when assigning from a non-OBT type to an OBT type, no warning is "
"issued as overflow behavior is being added, not discarded:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:648
msgid "-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-assignment-pedantic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:650
msgid ""
"A less severe version of `-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-"
"assignment` which is issued only when an unsigned `wrap` type is implicitly "
"converted to a standard unsigned integer type during assignment. This is "
"considered less problematic than other conversions because unsigned integers "
"already have well-defined wrapping behavior by the C standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:668
msgid ""
"This warning is useful for projects that want to track all overflow behavior "
"annotations but consider unsigned wrapping conversions to be lower priority "
"than signed conversions or `trap` conversions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:672
msgid "-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-function-boundary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:674
msgid ""
"This warning (disabled by default) is issued when an overflow behavior type "
"is passed as an argument to a function parameter that does not have the same "
"overflow behavior annotation. This helps identify situations where overflow "
"behavior contracts may be lost at function boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:691
msgid ""
"This warning can be particularly useful for catching cases where overflow "
"checking behavior is lost when crossing API boundaries. Both the general "
"version (`-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-function-boundary`) and a "
"pedantic version (`-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-function-boundary-"
"pedantic`) for unsigned wrapping types are disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:698
msgid "To fix this warning, you can either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:700
msgid "Update the function parameter to accept the overflow behavior type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:711
msgid ""
"Explicitly cast at the call site to acknowledge the loss of overflow "
"behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:722
msgid "-Wimplicit-overflow-behavior-conversion-function-boundary-pedantic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:724
msgid ""
"A less severe version of the warning above which is issued only in the case "
"of unsigned `wrap` types being passed to a function expecting a standard "
"unsigned integer type. This is a less problematic issue since the standard "
"and well-defined overflow procedure for unsigned integer types is "
"essentially `wrap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:730
msgid "Format String Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:732
msgid ""
"When overflow behavior types are used with format string functions (printf-"
"family functions like `printf`, `fprintf`, `sprintf`, etc., and scanf-family "
"functions like `scanf`, `fscanf`, `sscanf`, etc.), they are treated based on "
"their underlying integer types for format specifier compatibility checking. "
"More generally, overflow behavior types are ABI-compatible with their "
"underlying types when passed to any varargs function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:756
msgid ""
"This behavior ensures that overflow behavior types work seamlessly with "
"existing format string functions without requiring special format "
"specifiers, while still maintaining their overflow behavior semantics in "
"arithmetic operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:760
msgid ""
"The format string checker uses the underlying type to determine "
"compatibility, so `int __ob_wrap` is fully compatible with `%d`, `%i`, `%x`, "
"etc., just like a regular `int` would be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:764
msgid "Incompatibility With Non-Integer Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../OverflowBehaviorTypes.md:766
msgid ""
"An error is issued when attempting to create an overflow behavior type from "
"a non-integer type."
msgstr ""
